7. What is a Singleton Class and When to Use It:
A Singleton class ensures only one instance of the class exists. Used when one object is needed to coordinate actions across the system (e.g., database connection).
8. Create Singleton Class:
Example of a thread-safe Singleton class:
java
Copy
public class Singleton {
    private static Singleton instance;

    private Singleton() {}

    public static Singleton getInstance() {
        if (instance == null) {
            synchronized (Singleton.class) {
                if (instance == null) {
                    instance = new Singleton();
                }
            }
        }
        return instance;
    }
}
